          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the iron for the way you actually iron. For most homes that is the Rowenta Focus Excel DW5280, or the Black+Decker Allure D3030 if you want to spend less, both with stainless plates and three-way shut-off. Heavy ironers should look at a steam station, and people who mostly refresh hanging clothes may be happiest with a handheld steamer.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, the habits matter as much as the hardware: match the heat to the fabric, empty the tank after each session, and run the self-clean or descale routine every few weeks. Do that and a good iron will keep steaming cleanly for years.
          </p>
